{"task_id": "HumanEval/39", "solution": "def prime_fib(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    prime_fib returns n-th number that is a Fibonacci number and it's also prime.\n    >>> prime_fib(1)\n    2\n    >>> prime_fib(2)\n    3\n    >>> prime_fib(3)\n    5\n    >>> prime_fib(4)\n    13\n    >>> prime_fib(5)\n    89\n    \"\"\"\n    prime_memo = {}\n\n    def is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if a number is prime using trial division and memoization.\"\"\"\n        if num in prime_memo:\n            return prime_memo[num]\n\n        if num <= 1:\n            result = False\n        elif num == 2:\n            result = True\n        elif num % 2 == 0:\n            result = False\n        else:\n            is_prime_flag = True\n            i = 3\n            while i * i <= num:\n                if num % i == 0:\n                    is_prime_flag = False\n                    break\n                i += 2\n            result = is_prime_flag\n\n        prime_memo[num] = result\n        return result\n\n    found_count = 0\n    a, b = 0, 1  # Initialize Fibonacci sequence with F(0) and F(1)\n\n    while True:\n        # Generate the next Fibonacci number\n        next_fib = a + b\n        a = b\n        b = next_fib\n\n        # Skip numbers less than or equal to 1, as they are not prime.\n        # The problem examples start with 2 (F(3) if F(0)=0, F(1)=1)\n        # So we effectively skip 0, 1, 1 from being considered as prime_fib results.\n        if next_fib <= 1:\n            continue\n\n        # Check if the generated Fibonacci number is prime.\n        if is_prime(next_fib):\n            found_count += 1\n            if found_count == n:\n                return next_fib"}
