{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "def change_base(x: int, base: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    return string representation after the conversion.\n    base numbers are less than 10.\n    >>> change_base(8, 3)\n    '22'\n    >>> change_base(8, 2)\n    '1000'\n    >>> change_base(7, 2)\n    '111'\n    \"\"\"\n    if x == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    result_digits = []\n    current_x = x\n    while current_x > 0:\n        remainder = current_x % base\n        result_digits.append(str(remainder))\n        current_x //= base\n\n    return \"\".join(result_digits[::-1])"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the Fib4 number sequence.\n    This function efficiently calculates fib4(n) iteratively without recursion.\n    \"\"\"\n    initial_values = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n < len(initial_values):\n        return initial_values[n]\n\n    # Initialize with the base values: fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n    a, b, c, d = initial_values[0], initial_values[1], initial_values[2], initial_values[3]\n\n    # Iterate from n=4 up to the desired 'n'\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib = a + b + c + d\n        a, b, c, d = b, c, d, next_fib # Shift values to prepare for the next iteration\n\n    return d"}
